1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,088
An editor can change a page without changing what visitors see.

2
00:00:05,088 --> 00:00:09,473
In this video, you save changes as a draft, preview them, publish or

3
00:00:09,473 --> 00:00:11,903
discard them, and unpublish a page.

4
00:00:11,903 --> 00:00:15,280
Then you find the drafts that wait for publication.

5
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:24,176
A content item, such as an article, can have more than one version.

6
00:00:24,176 --> 00:00:27,236
The published version is the one visitors see.

7
00:00:27,236 --> 00:00:31,590
A draft is a version you are working on, and visitors cannot see it.

8
00:00:32,340 --> 00:00:36,260
When you edit a published item and save a draft, the published version

9
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:37,343
stays as it is.

10
00:00:37,343 --> 00:00:39,716
Your changes go into a separate version.

11
00:00:39,716 --> 00:00:44,410
Publishing the draft makes it the live one, and the version it replaces stays stored.

12
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:49,439
The Content Items list shows the state of each item with badges.

13
00:00:49,439 --> 00:00:52,129
Published means a live version exists.

14
00:00:52,129 --> 00:00:57,020
Draft means the last saved version is not live, and an item can show both.

15
00:00:57,770 --> 00:01:00,669
Two settings of a content type control this.

16
00:01:00,669 --> 00:01:06,642
Draftable adds the Save Draft button, and Versionable keeps the published version while you edit.

17
00:01:06,642 --> 00:01:10,700
Types you create in the admin have both, and so does the Article

18
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:12,150
type in this video.

19
00:01:16,415 --> 00:01:22,471
In Content, Content Items, the About article is published, and its row shows the Published badge.

20
00:01:22,471 --> 00:01:25,175
Let's click Edit to change its subtitle.

21
00:01:26,095 --> 00:01:27,996
The Edit Article page opens.

22
00:01:27,996 --> 00:01:31,125
Let's change the Subtitle to a different sentence.

23
00:01:31,125 --> 00:01:36,435
In the bottom bar, Publish would make the change live, so let's click Save Draft instead.

24
00:01:36,897 --> 00:01:40,180
Save Draft returns to the list, with the message:

25
00:01:40,180 --> 00:01:42,568
Your Article draft has been saved.

26
00:01:42,568 --> 00:01:47,046
The row shows two badges, Published and Draft, because the item has a

27
00:01:47,046 --> 00:01:48,897
live version and a draft.

28
00:01:49,353 --> 00:01:52,029
Let's click View to open the live page.

29
00:01:52,029 --> 00:01:57,323
The subtitle is the original text, because visitors see only the published version.

30
00:01:57,787 --> 00:02:00,659
Back in the list, let's click Preview Draft.

31
00:02:00,659 --> 00:02:05,253
It opens the draft in a separate tab, where the subtitle shows the change.

32
00:02:05,253 --> 00:02:08,297
Only users who may preview content can open it.

33
00:02:12,501 --> 00:02:16,165
Back in the list, let's open the Actions menu of the About row

34
00:02:16,165 --> 00:02:17,782
and click Publish Draft.

35
00:02:17,782 --> 00:02:21,446
The draft becomes the published version, and the message says:

36
00:02:21,446 --> 00:02:23,493
That Article has been published.

37
00:02:23,493 --> 00:02:25,271
The Draft badge disappears.

38
00:02:25,730 --> 00:02:28,459
Let's click View to open the live page again.

39
00:02:28,459 --> 00:02:32,740
It shows the changed subtitle, because the draft is the published version.

40
00:02:33,193 --> 00:02:35,811
Next, a change that you decide not to keep.

41
00:02:35,811 --> 00:02:39,552
Let's go back to the list, edit the Subtitle once more, and save

42
00:02:39,552 --> 00:02:40,888
it with Save Draft.

43
00:02:40,888 --> 00:02:43,133
The row shows the Draft badge again.

44
00:02:43,636 --> 00:02:47,105
Discard Draft, in the same menu, asks you to confirm.

45
00:02:47,105 --> 00:02:49,692
After you click Yes, the message says:

46
00:02:49,692 --> 00:02:52,103
The Article draft has been removed.

47
00:02:52,103 --> 00:02:57,336
The row shows only the Published badge again, and the live page was never affected.

48
00:03:01,576 --> 00:03:05,600
In the Actions menu of the About row, Unpublish takes the page out

49
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:08,506
of public view, and asks you to confirm first.

50
00:03:08,506 --> 00:03:10,966
After you click Yes, the message says:

51
00:03:10,966 --> 00:03:13,146
The Article has been unpublished.

52
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:15,370
The item is not deleted.

53
00:03:15,370 --> 00:03:19,499
Its row shows only the Draft badge, and the View button is gone,

54
00:03:19,499 --> 00:03:21,740
because no version is published.

55
00:03:22,201 --> 00:03:26,285
Publish Draft, in the Actions menu, puts the page back on the site.

56
00:03:26,285 --> 00:03:30,481
The row shows the Published badge again, and the View button returns.

57
00:03:34,695 --> 00:03:37,659
As the list grows, drafts can go unnoticed.

58
00:03:37,659 --> 00:03:41,287
Parking Information has a Published and a Draft badge:

59
00:03:41,287 --> 00:03:42,920
its draft is waiting.

60
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:47,395
Spring Event has only a Draft badge, so it has no published version.

61
00:03:47,853 --> 00:03:52,279
Let's open the Filters menu, the funnel button next to the search box,

62
00:03:52,279 --> 00:03:54,201
and click Only draft items.

63
00:03:54,201 --> 00:03:59,209
The list shows every item that has a draft, with or without a published version:

64
00:03:59,209 --> 00:04:02,063
here, Parking Information and Spring Event.

65
00:04:06,263 --> 00:04:09,296
Saving a draft needs permission to edit content.

66
00:04:09,296 --> 00:04:15,138
Publishing, publishing a draft and unpublishing need permission to publish content, and discarding

67
00:04:15,138 --> 00:04:17,890
a draft needs permission to delete content.

68
00:04:17,890 --> 00:04:22,103
A user who can only edit prepares changes that someone else releases.

69
00:04:22,853 --> 00:04:27,816
Older versions stay in the database, and Content Version Pruning can remove them.

70
00:04:27,816 --> 00:04:31,923
When the Audit Trail module is enabled and set to record a content

71
00:04:31,923 --> 00:04:37,000
type, it records that type's changes and can restore a recorded version as a draft.

72
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,883
Separate videos cover both.

73
00:04:40,883 --> 00:04:45,263
Save Draft keeps the live page as it is, and Publish Draft, Discard

74
00:04:45,263 --> 00:04:48,323
Draft and Unpublish decide what happens next.

75
00:04:48,323 --> 00:04:49,883
Thanks for watching.

